{% elif profile == 'packaged' %}meds-model preprocess_data external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
meds-model predict         input_data_dir=runs/data external_labels_dir=$LABELS_DIR output_predictions_dir=runs/predictions
{% else %}meds-model preprocess_data external_meds_dir=$MEDS_ROOT output_data_dir=runs/data
# ... then the commands listed by `meds-model commands`
{% endif %}```

Any extra argument is a Hydra override, e.g.
`meds-model supervised_train trainer.max_epochs=50 model.d_model=128`.

### Two rules worth knowing

**Sources are alternatives, not layers.** `supervised_train` and `predict` each accept several optional
input artifacts. Supplying more than one is an error rather than a precedence decision, and supplying one
the model does not handle is an error rather than a silently ignored argument.

**Predictions cover the whole index.** `predict` writes one row per task timepoint in the selected splits,
or fails. A short predictions file is indistinguishable downstream from a complete one, so it is never
written. Restrict the request with `splits=[held_out]` instead.

`predict` emits `predictions.parquet` in the
[meds-evaluation](https://github.com/kamilest/meds-evaluation) `PredictionSchema`
(`subject_id, prediction_time, predicted_boolean_probability`). **This repository ends at predicted
probabilities — it never reads ground-truth labels, and evaluation is a separate, shared tool.**

## Editing

**Start here: `src/{{ model_slug }}/model.py` is a stub.** The template generated the command DAG, not the
model — every hook in it raises `NotImplementedError` until you write it, and the docstring lists exactly
which hooks this DAG calls. Delete the `is_stub` marker when you are done.

{% if profile in ['zero_shot_direct', 'packaged'] %}- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/predict.py`** — also a stub: how this model answers a task.
{% endif %}- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/commands.py`** — which commands this model supports.
- **`src/{{ model_slug }}/configs/`** — `model/` constructor arguments, `paths/` locations, `profile/` the DAG.
- **`src/meds_model_base/`** — the vendored contract (managed by `copier update`; don't edit). It holds
  the command graph, manifests, schemas and a small MEDS-batch adapter layer — no models.

## Testing

```bash
uv run pytest -m "not slow"    # CLI smoke + the end-to-end conformance test
uv run pytest -m slow          # designed-signal learnability, with a negative control
```

The tests that need a working model **skip while `model.py` is a stub**, naming what to implement. They are
not scaffolding to delete — they are the contract your model has to satisfy, and they start running the
moment you remove the `is_stub` marker. A fresh repository is therefore green but honest: the CLI, config
composition and dispatcher are genuinely tested; the model is not yet there to test.

## Updating the template

```bash
copier update
```
